            <ArticleTitle>Combined spontaneous postpartum coronary artery dissection and pulmonary embolism with survival.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>29-33</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A young woman who survived after suffering in the immediate postpartum period a spontaneous coronary dissection with resultant myocardial infarction and a pulmonary embolism with pulmonary infarct is presented. Diagnostic and therapeutic considerations for this unique occurrence are discussed and reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
